ckson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","review_id":"mkmjXjh927cvCgkn7-U1dw","date":"2017-03-18T21:29:18","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9617122411727905,"text_excerpt":"This is the best meal I've had in NOLA, and I've been to many of the greats like Antoine's, Bayona, etc. They're slaying over at Cochon. We watched a clip on Eater, and since my babe loves all things barbecue, we wanted to drop in for a meal. Surprisingly, we ended up eating everything BUT the pork entree which people raved about on Eater. The space is awesome, with a handful of tables outdoors, and an excellent bar stocked with a vast array of Bourbon. My babe ordered a $30 Buffalo Trace Antique Collection (Stagg) Bourbon which he said was really hard to find. He took a lot of pleasure in sniffing and sipping upon it. Me? Well, I'm a cheap date. I ordered an old fashioned with Rye whiske..."},{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","review_id":"AY2OBvPveGGVBxFEg3eoLQ","date":"2011-07-28T00:12:38","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9565125107765198,"text_excerpt":"My husband and I were visiting New Orleans and we were on the hunt for delicious dinner fare, thank goodness we came across Cochon. We made a reservation for 8:30 on a Tuesday and as we walked up the street all of the surrounding restaurants were deserted. Cochon was absolutely busting at the seams, always a great sign! The interior sounds terrible on paper, but is really cool looking. It is a mix of wood, plaster, brick, and metal but it is very inviting and interesting to look at. The place is very open and it was fun seeing the kitchen and the plates being expedited. We decided on a few small plates and were absolutely delighted. Here is a run down of our meal: Fried alligator with chi..."},{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","review_id":"jQKGjRNQ9G273rXvUwp0cQ","date":"2014-10-06T14:38:05","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9502389430999756,"text_excerpt":"Cochon was the most recommended place to try on our trip to New Orleans, and it did not disappoint. The cocktail list was nice, and the bartender was very sweet and helpful. We started out with the pork cheeks and fried alligator. Get the pork cheeks and skip the alligator. The highlight of the meal was actually a special, and it was the pork shoulder served over puréed squash. It was an insanely well prepared and perfectly cooked meal. However, it was a special and I would be sad about not being able to get it if I returned. I do think the place may be a bit over hyped, as I had a slightly better meal at cafe Amelie the next night. For example, the bread they bring out at Cochon are thes..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","photo_id":"rxfc9gW1WJnNSlicezZuFA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/rxfc9gW1WJnNSlicezZuFA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8770326972007751},{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","photo_id":"2FkDdlzqg9LdkhppWswoBA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/2FkDdlzqg9LdkhppWswoBA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8640052676200867},{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","photo_id":"CLy_8RmrQGk4N9HjDwxKXw","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/CLy_8RmrQGk4N9HjDwxKXw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8186450004577637},{"business_id":"6a4gLLFSgr-Q6CZXDLzBGQ","photo_id":"LNLC308euyM00mZdVuBZcw","label"